Create one decorative title frame for the Urkaaaz Loadout screen.

## Reference

- Attach the full-screen Loadout screenshot as the primary visual reference.
- Match its dark translucent panels, warm gold trim, softly rounded corners,
  painterly fantasy atmosphere, and restrained highlights.
- Treat the screenshot as a style and proportion reference only. Do not copy
  its card art, characters, text, icons, or complete screen composition.

## Composition and use

- Create one compact, wide horizontal banner intended to sit above the three
  Loadout category panels on a landscape Android screen.
- Give the frame two centered, vertically stacked text areas:
  - a prominent title line for `LOADOUT`;
  - a smaller subtitle line for `CAMPAIGN LEVEL` followed by the current
    campaign level number.
- The level number is dynamic (`X` is a placeholder), so do not bake any
  number or lettering into the image. Keep both text areas clear and dark
  enough for Android to render the exact live strings over them in the game's
  Cinzel SemiBold font.
- Keep the banner visually balanced and compact. Its outer trim must not
  dominate the text or intrude into the category panels below it.
- Use a subtly textured, dark translucent interior with fine warm-gold edging
  and restrained corner ornaments. Keep the center uncluttered for legible
  live text.
- Make the banner's silhouette and ornamentation consistent with the
  screenshot's Loadout panels and selected-card accents, but do not imitate a
  card frame or add selected-state decoration.
- The banner should read clearly over both bright and dark areas of the
  existing background.

## Output

- Output exactly one PNG: `loadout_header_frame.png`.
- Canvas: 1024 x 256 pixels, RGBA with transparent pixels outside the frame.
- Use a centered, wide composition with even transparent margins.
- Save the file for review under `assets_src/loadout/ui/`.
- Do not copy it into Android resources until the user approves the preview.
- The image is a presentation asset only; do not change screen behavior or
  encode a fixed campaign level in the artwork.

## Review checklist

- Verify the file is a valid 1024 x 256 RGBA PNG with transparency outside the
  banner.
- Preview it over the full-screen Loadout screenshot at its intended size.
- Confirm there is a clear title area for `LOADOUT` and a separate subtitle
  area for `CAMPAIGN LEVEL` plus a live level number.
- Check that margins and ornaments are balanced and that the frame does not
  crowd the category panels.
- Ensure there is no text, number, logo, card art, icon, watermark, or
  signature baked into the asset.
- Show the preview for user review before Android integration.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, numbers, words, fixed campaign level, logo, watermark,
signature, screenshot, full-screen composition, card grid, ammunition art,
spell art, unit art, selected border, checkmark, infinity icon, lock icon,
oversized heavy frame, busy center, opaque rectangular background, uneven
transparent margins, unrelated franchise, photorealistic UI mockup
